    <p class="lead">
      Under the Scotland Acts of 2012 and 2016, the Scottish Parliament holds devolved powers to set Income Tax rates and band thresholds on non-savings and non-dividend income for individuals living in Scotland. As a result, taxpayers in Scotland experience a distinctly different tax structure compared to taxpayers in England, Wales, and Northern Ireland (rUK). If you live, work, or run a business that crosses the Anglo-Scottish border, understanding these nuances is critical for effective financial planning and peace of mind.
    </p>
    
