    <p>
      As the table illustrates, an individual earning £50,000 will find themselves over £1,500 worse off annually in Scotland. For senior executives and highly qualified professionals earning £100,000, the gap widens to nearly £4,600. This disparity has sparked intense debate among businesses operating cross-border, with many citing difficulties in recruiting talent to Scottish offices without offering "equalization" bonuses to offset the higher tax burden.
    </p>

